<title>SINGAPORE: Sri Lanka offers early September naphtha by tender.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka offers early September naphtha by tender.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's state-owned Ceylon Petroleum Corp (CPC) has issued a tender to sell 125,000-barrels of naphtha lifting September 8-9 from Colombo, a company official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes August 13 and offers are to be valid for two days.</p>
<p>In its last naphtha tender, CPC sold 125,000 barrels lifting July 18-19 to Dutch trader Vitol at 53 cents per barrel below Singapore spot quotes, on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870 3086)</p>
